SUMMARY:Inprint Marlon James Reading
DESCRIPTION:General admission tickets will go on sale on Tuesday\, March 16\, 2027 at 12 pm. Season tickets are on sale here. \nMarlon James will read from his new novel The Disappearers\, followed by an on-stage conversation led by a local author/journalist. The evening will conclude with a book sale and signing. The event is presented as part of the 2026/2027 Inprint Margarett Root Brown Reading Series.  \nMarlon James is the Booker Prize–winning and New York Times bestselling author of A Brief History of Seven Killings; the bestselling and National Book Award finalist Black Leopard\, Red Wolf; as well as the bestselling Moon Witch\, Spider King; The Book of Night Women; and John Crow’s Devil. In addition to the Booker Prize\, his novels have won the American Book Award\, the Anisfield-Wolf Book Award\, the Dayton Literary Peace Prize\, the OCM Bocas Prize for Caribbean Literature\, and the Los Angeles Times Ray Bradbury Prize for Science Fiction\, and have been finalists for the National Book Critics Circle Award and the NAACP Image Award. In 2019\, Time magazine named him one of the 100 most influential people in the world. \nJames joins Inprint with his new novel The Disappearers\, an unflinching exploration of queer life in Jamaica during the 1980s and 1990s. “Captivating and epic . . . James renders his characters’ tumultuous inner lives with striking imagery and energy; their dialogue is rapid\, keen\, and hard-hitting. In all\, a gritty\, powerful\, and gripping read” (Booklist). In 1988\, eight men in Kingston\, Jamaica\, begin rehearsals for a play. The men are strangers to one another\, but they all share one inescapable truth: all of them are gay. One night a mob savagely attacks them\, killing one of the men. For the survivors\, their recovery is as much emotional as it is physical. As their bodies heal\, each man grapples with the violence\, the hatred\, and the rage that the attack made plain. Some try to ignore what the attack has unearthed\, while others double down on retribution. In The Disappearers\, James has written a riveting and deeply human story of men forced to make compromises to survive what the society they live in demands. \n
URL:https://inprinthouston.org/event/inprint-marlon-james-reading/
LOCATION:Alley Theatre\, 615 Texas Avenue\, Houston\, TX\, 77002
CATEGORIES:2026/2027 Inprint Margarett Root Brown Reading Series
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://inprinthouston.org/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/Marlon-James-credit-Mark-Seliger-for-website.jpg
END:VEVENT
END:VCALENDAR